{
    "architecture": "aarch64",
    "context": "Native single-thread process-leader sched_attr nice contract: 29310 root/UID1000 checks per architecture; signed32 normalization, target RLIMIT_NICE, effective CAP_SYS_NICE independently of UID0, fair-class state application and nonfair nice preservation. Six target classes, guarded read-only/unaligned/inaccessible inputs, upper PID/flag words, layouts and real musl getpriority observations; privileged synchronous broker restores peer state. Separate original cohort failure vectors, identical-ELF Linux 6.12.51 references, 25 probe allocas and two warmed 200-cycle storage cohorts. Four production builds, exact complete C scope with only three uses of one compiler loop identifier per architecture renamed, eight cases with identical corrected kernels: ARM five primary plus three completion passes; x86 five primary plus two completion and one recovery pass, retaining the explicit p3 fcntlabi ENOSPC build failure with absent ISO/serial and matching recovery source/C/ELF. Missing initial aggregates, 117 interrupted files, 30 stopped-retry regular files and 67 p3 retained files remain explicit, executing audit negatives and independent lifetime review. Native nice remains process-wide; worker-thread nice, target/credential/limit races, complete realtime/deadline/reset/clamp behavior, GNU/foreign/ELF32 and broad roadmap gates remain open",
    "base_commit": "4fd5c605d87b05208b73cf725ba93b59699b4f1c",
